<title>USA: Disney to show animated films on ABC - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Disney to show animated films on ABC - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Disney will use its ABC television network as a showcase for its animated films next fall, The Wall Street Journal reported Monday.</p>
<p>The development marks a change in strategy, allowing the struggling network benefit from films like &quot;Toy Story&quot; and &quot;Pocahontas,&quot; the story said.</p>
<p>Disney acquired the network in 1995.</p>
<p>In the past, Disney has kept its animated films off network television with just a few exceptions, the story said.</p>
</text>
